univalue
------------------------------------------
A universal value object, with JSON encoding (output) and decoding (input).

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libunivalue-devel-1.1.1-1bl2
  libunivalue0-1.1.1-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.11-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/jgarzik/univalue

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/jgarzik/univalue/archive/refs/tags/v1.1.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack univalue-1.1.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./univalue-1.1.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/univalue-1.1.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/univalue-1.1.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libunivalue0-1.1.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libunivalue-devel-1.1.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(univalue)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/univalue.README
  /usr/share/doc/univalue/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/univalue/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/univalue/TODO

(libunivalue0)
  /usr/bin/cygunivalue-0.dll

(libunivalue-devel)
  /usr/include/univalue.h
  /usr/lib/libunivalue.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/libunivalue.pc

